It is completely reliable if you understand the mechanics of how it works.
If your alignment is greater than 0 (and even as a role that starts as 0,
kill something), you are Weak, and you haven't committed one of the
obvious divine faux pas, your god will fix a major problem (and so if
Weakness is your only one, you're home free). Every time. There's no
random element there aside from timeout, and...

... if you haven't increased timeout somehow (being crowned, being above
XL15, etc), the odds of it not having expired between two food prayers,
even with a pair of rings and no other nutrition, are _utterly_
miniscule.

Of course, it's nice to avoid praying for food at all, but the idea that
it's unreliable does not stand up to examination.
